Installed Docker
- Created a test HTML file, named file index.html
- Created a document called Dockerfile, pointing to the HTML file location
- Verified container is running via docker ps and docker image ls command
- Confirmed website is running by navigating to localIP: 127.0.0.1:80
Installed Kubernetes with kubectl and Minikube, to run locally
- Tied Minikube to work with docker, specified what internal port to use.
  - minikube start --driver=docker --ports=30080:30080
- Created a deployment.yaml file, to point to docker file, pointed minikube to runfile
- Created a services.yaml, specifying the Nodeport used during the install, pointed minikube to runfile
- Verified pod is running via kubectl get pod and kubectl get services, minikube service mywebsite --url command
- Can scale using kubectl scale deployment mywebsite --replicas=2



services.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: orange
spec:
  selector:
    app: orange
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 8080
      targetPort: 80
      nodePort: 30080
  type: NodePort

deployment.yaml

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: orange
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: orange
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: orange
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: orange
          image: orange
          imagePullPolicy: Never
          ports:
            - containerPort: 8080
          resources:
            requests:
              cpu: 100m
            limits:
              cpu: 500m
